<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="GameplayTagContainer" inherits="Resource" api_type="extension" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot/master/doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		An ordered set of gameplay tags, serialized as plain names.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Serializes as a [PackedStringArray] of tag names and resolves each name through [GameplayTagsManager] on load. That is deliberate: assets reference tags by name, so a tag can move between tables, or a table can be split, without touching anything that uses it.
		[method has_tag] honours the hierarchy - a container holding [code]A.B.C[/code] answers yes to [code]A.B[/code]. The exact variants do not.
	</description>
